        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1337">

                <pb facs="1143" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1039"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/542.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bundy Cole, manager of the National Bank of Nicaragua, left for the United States
                    April 22 to lay before the bankers the proposals for the new loan which the
                    Government is anxious to negotiate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Weitzel</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
